<group prefix="WebGpuSharp.">
    <comment location="SamplerBindingType">
        <summary>            
            Specific type of a sampler binding.
        </summary>
    </comment>
    <group prefix="SamplerBindingType.">
		<comment location="BindingNotUsed">
			<summary>
				Indicates that this <see cref="WebGpuSharp.SamplerBindingLayout"/> member of
     			its parent <see cref="WebGpuSharp.BindGroupLayoutEntry"/> is not used.
			</summary>
		</comment>
		<comment location="Undefined">
			<summary>No sampler binding type specified.</summary>
		</comment>
		<comment location="Filtering">
			<summary>The sampling result is produced based on more than a single color sample from a texture, e.g. when bilinear interpolation is enabled.</summary>
		</comment>
		<comment location="NonFiltering">
			<summary>The sampling result is produced based on a single color sample from a texture.</summary>
		</comment>
		<comment location="Comparison">
			<summary>
				Use as a comparison sampler instead of a normal sampler. 
				For more info take a look at the analogous functionality in <see href="https://www.khronos.org/opengl/wiki/Sampler_Object#Comparison_mode.">OpenGL</see>.
			</summary>
		</comment>
	</group>
</group>